# Rung 3's ENFORCED-3: hold the sandbox open so the HOST can ask the runtime what
# this sandbox stamps and whether it is tainted.
#
# The query needs a running sandbox. docker tears the runsc state directory down
# when the container exits, and a `runsc ladder-status` after that fails with
# "loading container: file does not exist". So the agent reads its labeled source,
# sends one message, and then blocks on a marker file the launcher drops when it has
# finished asking. Rung 1's attenuation check has the same shape and for the same
# reason.
#
# The agent gets no authority from the marker: it lands in a directory it can
# already read, and its arrival tells it nothing it could act on.

read-source /untrusted/injected-report.txt

send-agent --from-source /untrusted/injected-report.txt ops

wait-for /scratch/release --timeout 60
